{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The disputed SGD 5.00 is not in the rider's hands now: EV-FARE-05067 records the fee charged at 09:30:14 and refunded the same day, with payment_status = REFUNDED and refund_issued_sgd = 5.00, and the trip record's own event log shows the money was withheld from the driver pending this review. Under POL-GEN-03 the five ruling values are party-relative, and FULL_REFUND and PARTIAL_REFUND are defined against the FILER - here the driver, not the rider. The rider's win on this filing is therefore that the present state stands, which is exactly what NO_ACTION means; any ruling that moves money on this record moves it toward the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05067", "EV-TRIP-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The record tells us nothing about where the rider was. EV-GPS-05067 carries an empty rider_track, and its arrival check measures only the driver's own fixes against the recorded pickup coordinate; no artifact in the package shows the rider away from the pickup, unable to board, or refusing to board. A cancellation 'as a rider no-show' under POL-NS-21 turns on precisely that fact, and POL-GEN-26 requires that where a fact a rule needs cannot be established on the evidence, the case goes to a human reviewer and no outcome is inferred from the gap - its second sentence forbids exactly the inference the driver's filing asks for.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05067", "EV-TRIP-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.rider_track",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even the driver's arrival is proved only against a bare coordinate, not against this rider's block. The pickup carries venue_id = null in EV-TRIP-05067, and nothing in the record - no venue_id, and no party statement in the chat log - identifies that coordinate as the rider's block or entrance. POL-NS-21's arrival test in EV-GPS-05067 asks only whether the driver's fixes sat within the STANDARD zone radius of 50 m of that coordinate (nearest fix 1.81 m), and the arrival marker it corroborates is itself GPS-derived ('Auto-arrival from driver GPS', EV-TRIP-05067), so the trace is corroborating a marker drawn from the same device's own trace. The single question that matters - was the driver where this rider was waiting - is not settled by this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05067", "EV-GPS-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Any AI ruling on this dispute must be reached at 0.95 confidence. The rider's profile carries rider_profile.fraud_flags = 3 (EV-RPROF-05067), and POL-GEN-22 fixes the required confidence at 0.95 wherever a party's profile carries a fraud flag, whatever the dispute value; POL-NS-26 makes the no-show ruling expressly subject to that bar. The driver's filing asks the platform to undo an interim reversal and take SGD 5.00 back from a rider who is not now carrying it, on a record that resolves only the driver's half of the encounter. At a 0.95 bar the AI should not re-charge her, and the case belongs to a human reviewer.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.fraud_flags",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The one rider-favouring test on this policy is POL-NS-24, which measures the driver's lateness from the scheduled pickup time plus 5 minutes - and this trip has no scheduled time at all: driver_deadline.deadline is null in EV-TRIP-05067, for the stated reason 'on-demand trip: no scheduled time'. POL-NS-24's own note directs that where the record carries no scheduled time and the deadline cannot be fixed, POL-GEN-26 applies. The test that could have answered this case in the rider's favour therefore cannot be applied on this record, and that unresolved question goes to a human reviewer rather than to a re-charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.driver_deadline",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The record has no source outside the platform's own telemetry and the driver's own device: the only third-party artifact for this trip, the LTA traffic advisory, is absent. EV-ADVIS-05067-01 is MISSING, its issue codes are MISSING_ARTIFACT, and its weight is 0.0 - I disclose that impairment rather than present it as clean evidence. POL-GEN-02 makes the completeness of the evidence part of the confidence a ruling is held to, and on a filing that would move SGD 5.00 to the driver, the absence of any independent source tells against finality and against re-charging the rider on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05067-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I concede the contact obligation and do not build on it: EV-CHAT-05067 shows three in-app messages (09:22:00, 09:25:30, 09:28:40) and EV-TRIP-05067 shows two in-app calls (09:24:10, 09:27:20), every one of them before cancelled_at at 09:30:10, which is why the derived contact_before_cancel block records obligation_met = true. POL-NS-23 is satisfied on this record. The rider's case does not rest on it; it rests on the facts this record leaves unresolved - where the rider was, and whether the charge should be taken from her a second time.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05067", "EV-TRIP-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.obligation_met",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 5.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the driver and the rider. Trip TRP-05067 was an on-demand Ryde X booking from Block 680, Choa Chu Kang Crescent. The driver cancelled at 09:30:10 as a rider no-show, a 5.00 SGD fee was charged at 09:30:14, and at 10:46:10 that 5.00 SGD was returned to the rider and withheld from the driver pending this review. On this record the fee stands, so the 5.00 SGD moves back to the driver.\n\nWHY THE FEE STANDS. (1) POL-NS-21 (free wait): the trip record's arrival event at 09:21:45 is corroborated by the driver-device GPS trace — the nearest fix is 1.81 m from the recorded pickup coordinate (fix 13, 09:22:20, reported accuracy 6 m), well inside the 50 m radius for a STANDARD pickup — and the trace holds the vehicle at 0 kph from 09:21:50 through 09:29:50. This being an on-demand trip with no scheduled time, the 300 s free wait ran from arrival to 09:26:45; the driver cancelled at 09:30:10, 505 s after arrival, 205 s past expiry. (2) POL-NS-23 (contact): before cancelling the driver sent three in-app messages (09:22:00, 09:25:30, 09:28:40) and placed two in-app calls (09:24:10 and 09:27:20, both unanswered), so both limbs are met and the FULL_REFUND that clause attaches to a missed step is not engaged. (3) POL-NS-22 (the fee): 5.00 SGD was charged and fee_matches_policy is true; where the fee stands the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with both money fields equal to the fee charged, and under POL-GEN-03 amount_sgd carries the same figure as driver_compensation_sgd (5.00 SGD).\n\nTHE RIDER'S POINTS. Your account that the driver never came to your block is contradicted by the driver-device trace and nothing on the record supports it — rider_track is empty, so there is no rider-side location evidence at all. POL-GEN-26 escalates only where a fact a rule must have cannot be established; the facts the no-show rules need (arrival, the free wait, the messages and the calls before cancellation) are all established at full weight. POL-NS-24 (driver no-show) is the rider's remedy and is engaged only where the rider cancels because the driver failed to arrive; you did not cancel and the driver did arrive, so that clause is not in play, and its on-demand deadline gap does not leave a fact this ruling needs because POL-NS-21 supplies the on-demand treatment. The 10:46:10 reversal was a holding step pending review, not a final outcome, so the party-relative reading of POL-GEN-03 does not freeze it once the fee is found to stand. The absent LTA advisory (EV-ADVIS-05067-01, MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0) carries no fact, and no rule here requires traffic data, so it neither lowers confidence nor opens a question.\n\nThe driver's evidence points — arrival corroboration, the free wait, the contact steps, the 5.00 SGD amount, and that the record can bear the required confidence — are accepted; the contact obligation is common ground.\n\nCONFIDENCE. The rider's profile carries fraud_flags 3, so POL-GEN-22 (with POL-NS-26) requires 0.95. The artifacts carrying the deciding facts — trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare breakdown — are each COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the cap is 1.0 and this ruling issues at 0.95.\n\nNO REFERRAL APPLIES: the fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD policy fee (POL-NS-22 referral not triggered); the driver attempted contact, so the POL-NS-24 goodwill credit does not arise; and the rider's no_show_cancellations_30d of 1, counting this trip, reaches 2, below the POL-NS-25 threshold of 3."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Nothing here needs a human. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05067-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and so carries no fact at all. No rule in the no-show category requires traffic data, and every fact POL-NS-21, POL-NS-22 and POL-NS-23 need — arrival, the free wait, the fee charged, the messages and the calls before cancellation — is established on artifacts assessed COMPLETE at full weight. There is no open question of the kind POL-GEN-26 sends to a reviewer, and the absence of a third-party advisory is not evidence of anything.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-05067-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
